{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfcSk2c74WLaTDMcymzYK", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags here are read through `flags.is_on()`, and the code matches the stored convention.\n\n- **Declare the flag in `flags.toml`.** Add it under `[flags]` with a kebab-case name and a boolean default. The only flag today is `invoice-pdf-v2 = false`. For yours, add `new-checkout-flow = false`.\n- **Read it with `flags.is_on(\"new-checkout-flow\")`** from `src/flags.py`. Don't read the TOML or environment variables directly.\n- **Undeclared names are silently off.** `is_on` returns `False` for any name missing from `flags.toml`, so a typo in the name won't raise an error. It will just never turn on.\n- **Flags are static.** `flags.toml` is loaded once at import, so changing a flag means editing the file and restarting. There are no per-user rollouts or runtime toggles.\n- **`all_flags()` returns a copy of the full flag dict.** It's handy for debugging or for exposing flag state.\n\nA typical gate looks like this:\n\n```python\nfrom src import flags\n\nif flags.is_on(\"new-checkout-flow\"):\n    return new_checkout(cart)\nreturn legacy_checkout(cart)\n```\n\nI haven't looked at the existing checkout code. If you point me to it, I can add the flag and the branch. Run tests with `make test-fast`. I'd also add a test for each side of the flag."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1483, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24774, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1483}, "output_tokens": 455, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0ea7e4b5-027a-41f7-919d-baed5483af8a", "uuid": "b8126f02-735d-4711-a725-a34b825